    <dcterms:title>Dombey and Son</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description>Wikipedia page about this book: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dombey_and_Son</dcterms:description>
    <pgterms:marc508>Neil McLachlan, Ted Davis and David Widger</pgterms:marc508>
    <pgterms:marc520>"Dombey and Son" by Charles Dickens is a novel published in monthly parts between 1846 and 1848. It follows Paul Dombey, a wealthy shipping firm owner obsessed with having a son to inherit his business, who coldly neglects his devoted daughter Florence. When tragedy strikes and his dreams crumble, Dombey's pride leads him through a loveless second marriage, betrayal, and family ruin. The story explores themes of parental rejection, social class, and the destructive nature of pride in Victorian England. (This is an automatically generated summary.)</pgterms:marc520>
    <pgterms:marc908>Reading ease score: 75.2 (7th grade). Fairly easy to read.</pgterms:marc908>
